        <mxCell id="n15" value="The risk rule is the phase's own proof of a claim the previous phase made: adding a&#10;second kind of hazard is one new file and one added line, with nothing else touched.&#10;That is visible in the commit itself, which is why the plan makes the shape of the diff&#10;part of the acceptance rather than a matter of style." style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;html=1;fillColor=#f2f4f9;strokeColor=#e3e5ea;fontColor=#3d3d46;fontSize=15.4;align=left;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="428" width="700" height="93.6" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
